PATCHES APPLIED DURING THIS RUN:

Patch: seed-demo-shops.ts — softDeleteProductVariants() before softDeleteProducts()

Root cause: Medusa's softDeleteProducts() does NOT cascade to product_variant rows.
The unique SKU constraint on product_variant is not filtered by deleted_at, so when the
seed tried to re-create a product with the same SKU, it failed with:
  "Product variant with sku: HK-MARGHERITA-PIZZA, already exists."

Fix applied: In the idempotency cleanup block (Step 4 of the seed), the query now fetches
"variants.id" alongside the product id, then calls:
  await productSvc.softDeleteProductVariants(variantIds)
before calling softDeleteProducts(). This explicitly frees the SKU constraint and allows
clean re-creation on subsequent runs.

The variant unique constraint in Medusa appears to check against all rows (including
soft-deleted rows from OTHER prior runs), but since productSvc.softDeleteProductVariants()
was called in the patched seed, the re-run succeeded cleanly with count = 32.
